[[0,2219909,0,1,0,1,"2017-11-01T00:29:16","madmalloy","",[],"","Antifa Set To Terrorize America: Objective Is To Cause Civil Unrest And Initiate Rioting In Many Major American Cities","http://www.shtfplan.com/headline-news/antifa-set-to-terrorize-america-objective-is-to-cause-civil-unrest-and-initiate-rioting-in-many-major-american-cities_10312017","Conspiracy"],[1,10936582,0,0,0,0,"2017-11-01T00:58:18","BestCaseOntario","",[],"<p>Paid for by your local three letter agency. Don't let the Soros front fool you. The US could stop this shit in a heartbeat if they wanted to. Agitprop - coming to a city near you.</p>"],[1,10938166,0,0,0,0,"2017-11-01T04:26:35","Fiveonit","",[],"<p>Well the recent truck of peace attack will have police on high alert throughout the country so good luck with that.</p>\n<p>inb4 truck of peace was a false flag.</p>"],[2,10938735,10938166,0,0,0,"2017-11-01T05:59:08","Greenzero86","",[],"<p>Truck of peace was probably a distraction.</p>"],[3,10940781,10938735,2,0,2,"2017-11-01T14:17:27","Ohsoedgy","",[],"<p>Right. False Flags usually involve whites and kids.</p>"],[1,10942760,0,0,0,0,"2017-11-01T18:24:40","jervybingly","",[],"<p>Is Soros above the law?</p>"]]
[[0,2219910,0,56,0,56,"2017-11-01T00:31:43","Bad-R0nald","",[],"","High school students are protesting the Pledge of Allegiance, and now schools are getting sued","https://www.theblaze.com/news/2017/10/31/high-school-students-are-protesting-the-pledge-of-allegiance-and-now-schools-are-getting-sued","news"],[1,10937040,0,0,0,0,"2017-11-01T01:52:59","Fambida","",[],"<p>I realise some folks won't agree with me on this, but this is good. Sitting during the pledge is just as much a free speech right as kneeling for the anthem. And those people can suffer the consequences or lack thereof from other citizens for their actions just like the football kneelers.</p>"],[2,10939224,10937040,0,0,0,"2017-11-01T07:55:28","BlackSheepBrouhaha","",[],"<p>In school, I stood for the pledge, but did not say it. My allegiance is not to the flag, state, or republic. My allegiance is to myself, my family, my community, and my faith. </p>\n<p>Faith is just the word I use to mean belief in the absence of perfect knowledge. The less faith I need, the better. But I'm not afraid to act on faith, and I'm willing to defend it more than the interests of the government.</p>"],[1,10937395,0,0,0,0,"2017-11-01T02:40:05","Samsquamch","",[],"<blockquote>\n<p>M.O. said she sits for the pledge because it’s her constitutional right, and also because “we live in a country where there isn’t justice and freedom for all, so I’m not going to stand for a pledge that says there is when there really isn’t.”</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Translation: She lives in a country where she has constitutional rights and can do what she pleases with those rights. But she thinks she lives in a country where she doesn't have those rights, even though they are what allows her to sit and voice her opposing opinion.</p>\n<p>That said, schools have rules, unfortunately, and they need to be followed. Your classmates don't get the freedom to insult you, and you don't get the freedom to openly stand against your country while attending a public institution of education provided by that country.</p>"],[2,10937743,10937395,0,0,0,"2017-11-01T03:27:01","LongyyBearr","",[],"<blockquote>\n<p>you don't get the freedom to openly stand against your country while attending a public institution of education provided by that country.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Pin the tail on the ugly donkey now</p>"],[3,10938598,10937743,0,0,0,"2017-11-01T05:41:24","Samsquamch","",[],"<p>While at work, do you get to insult your co-workers? If they're from a different country, do you get to disrespect their countries without any consequences?</p>\n<p>That's my point - Even at a government job, there are rules. I don't necessarily agree with all of them, but I understand they need to be followed if I want to work there. Schools are no different - Everyone prefers a different set of rules, but by attending, you've also agreed to follow the rules that are in place. If you don't agree, attend a private school that you DO agree with. Just don't expect tax dollars to pay for it.</p>"],[2,10938182,10937395,1,0,1,"2017-11-01T04:28:30","badruns","",[],"<p>Sure you do. You're legally obligated to attend school, you aren't legally obligated to say a pledge. It's foolish for a school to try to enforce a pledge, because they will get sued and they will lose.</p>\n<p>The great thing about America is yes, you have the freedom to say what you want. It was designed that way for good reason. If you don't support their right to not say the pledge, I'm not so sure you understand the effort put in by the founding fathers.</p>"],[3,10938637,10938182,0,0,0,"2017-11-01T05:45:17","Samsquamch","[e]",[],"<p>You're not legally obligated to attend school with a national anthem. You can attend a private school or be home schooled, both of which do NOT require you stand for the national anthem. </p>\n<p>The pledge of allegiance is stupid, but it's part of the rules. Public schools are there to prepare children and young adults for the public world, which includes following rules you don''t agree with at times.</p>"],[4,10939120,10938637,0,0,0,"2017-11-01T07:20:02","myvoicefromhell","",[],"<p>Wrong. The first amendment protects these kids, too, and that includes being able to choose not to say the pledge. Silence is protected speech whether you like it or not and is recognized by federal law as such.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://s1.postimg.org/6lgj2ssbm7/Screenshot_2017-11-01-00-17-43.png\">https://s1.postimg.org/6lgj2ssbm7/Screenshot_2017-11-01-00-17-43.png</a></p>\n<p>The school is going to lose.</p>"],[1,10938322,0,0,0,0,"2017-11-01T04:56:08","XxSanityIsSanityxX","",[],"<p>The Pledge Of Allegiance was incorporated into the school system via a marketing company to sell flags.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://priceonomics.com/the-marketing-of-the-pledge-of-allegiance/\">Link</a></p>"],[2,10938723,10938322,0,0,0,"2017-11-01T05:57:38","Greenzero86","",[],"<blockquote>\n<p>marketing company to sell flags.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Ironically, it was written by a Christian socialist.</p>"],[3,10939341,10938723,0,0,0,"2017-11-01T08:43:33","XxSanityIsSanityxX","",[],"<p><a href=\"https://youtube.com/watch?v=GiCaqA0ngRc\">Shhhh, don't question the narrative</a></p>"],[1,10938802,0,0,0,0,"2017-11-01T06:09:03","TrueAmerican","",[],"<p>good, if i had a high school kid, i would tell them not to stand and would show them how to take legal action when an authoritative figure violates their constitutional rights. Clog up the legal system with bullshit, beat them at their own game.</p>"],[1,10939534,0,0,0,0,"2017-11-01T09:44:09","Nathan_Explosion","[e]",[],"<p>Are these &quot;diverse&quot; students or students from a household headed by a liberal parent? I'm just curious.</p>"]]
